From 65b4315526bcd3b714f0fcabf2819d01ebf406d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Ruiz <github@xav.ie>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:42:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Trim successful call and execute results to what the agent
 needs

A single direct call that succeeds returns its value alone instead of
{ path, ok, value }; a batch and a failure keep that shape. A call's MCP result
whose content is all text sends only its structuredContent, the same data the
text repeats; an error or other content keeps the whole result. Programs in
execute still receive whole results.

A completed execution leaves out toolCalls when every call succeeded, and keeps
the list when one failed, was interrupted or waits for approval. The call
description, the executor skill and the e2e expectations follow the new shapes.
